{"summary":"Fix exact-capacity error formatting for positive and negative error codes.","explanation":"The checked-in test formats error codes 42 and -1 with a prefix so `prefix + sep + msg` is exactly `inline_buffer_size` bytes (500). It expects that full expression in `to_string(buffer)` and `size` to equal `buffer.size()`. The current strict `<` rejects the exact-fit prefix, leaving only `error 42` or `error -1` (8 bytes). For negative codes, the size calculation also reserves two bytes for the sign although the rendered sign occupies one, rejecting a prefix that fits. Allow the exact boundary and count the negative sign as one byte; the existing fallback still handles a prefix that exceeds capacity.","edits":[{"path":"include/fmt/format-inl.h","old":"  if (detail::is_negative(error_code)) {
    abs_value = 0 - abs_value;
    error_code_size += 2;
  }
  error_code_size += detail::to_unsigned(detail::count_digits(abs_value));
  auto it = appender(out);
  if (message.size() < inline_buffer_size - error_code_size)","new":"  if (detail::is_negative(error_code)) {
    abs_value = 0 - abs_value;
    error_code_size += 1;
  }
  error_code_size += detail::to_unsigned(detail::count_digits(abs_value));
  auto it = appender(out);
  if (message.size() <= inline_buffer_size - error_code_size)"}]}
